WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.860
In 1934, the Swiss theologian Karl Barth was
the main author of the Barmen Declaration.

2
00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.900
It rejected Nazi control of the Church.

3
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:14.010
A year later, Barth was
dismissed from his post at Bonn.

4
00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.670
Decades later, in multi-faith Birmingham,

5
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.190
the philosopher John Hick
asked a different question.

6
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.930
What can Christians honestly believe,
after the atrocities of the 20th century?

7
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:30.070
So on the cross, did God
take our place in court?

8
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.330
Or did Jesus simply show us how to love?

9
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.360
In this mission, you'll
step into Barth's courtroom,

10
00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:38.270
built in 4 steps.

11
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.450
Then you'll test Hick's claim
that God incarnate is a metaphor.

12
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.560
Your mission: compare how Barth
and Hick understand the cross,

13
00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:48.120
and weigh up their strengths.
